{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}BugOut Index — {{ snapshot.bugout_index }} · {{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}{% endblock %}
{% block body %}

<section class="hero">
  <div>{{ gauge|safe }}</div>
  <div>
    <div class="label">Week of {{ snapshot.publication_date }}</div>
    <h2>{{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}</h2>
    <div class="sub">{{ snapshot.interpretation.risk }}. A directional reading of six published statistics against fixed endpoints, as one 0–100 score. Higher means less stress. Not a forecast, and not an instruction to bug out.</div>
    <span class="band {{ snapshot.interpretation.band_key }}">{{ snapshot.interpretation.band }}</span>
    <div class="delta">
      {% if boi_delta is not none %}
        Week-over-week: <strong>{{ "%+.2f"|format(boi_delta) }}</strong> points
      {% else %}
        Week-over-week: <strong>first recorded week</strong>
      {% endif %}
      · {{ history_count }} week(s) of history
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if week_note %}
<section class="week-note" aria-label="What changed this week">
  <h3>This week</h3>
  {% for sentence in week_note %}
  <p{% if loop.last %} class="disclaimer"{% endif %}>{{ sentence }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Core metrics</h3>
  <span class="hint">Each tile shows the raw value, how old that reading is, the normalized 0–100 score, and the raw weight (weights sum to 0.72; see Methodology for shares of the finished index).</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  Headline labor numbers move after release. See how much the last 24 months of payrolls
  have been revised on the <a href="./revisions.html">data revisions tracker</a>.
</p>
<div class="grid metrics">
  {% for m in metrics %}
  <div class="tile{% if m.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ m.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ m.raw|fmt(m.unit) }}</div>
    {{ m.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="norm-bar"><span style="width: {{ m.normalized or 0 }}%"></span></div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Normalized {{ (m.normalized if m.normalized is not none else '—') }} / 100</span>
      <span>Raw weight {{ m.weight_pct }}%</span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ m.source_url }}">{{ m.source }}</a></span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ m.age_text }}{% if m.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    {% if m.diagnostics and not m.diagnostics.index_input %}
    <div class="age">Candidate {{ m.diagnostics.candidate_incident_rate }} per 100k for {{ m.diagnostics.candidate_month }} (population-weighted {{ m.diagnostics.population_weighted_incident_rate }}). Not an index input; the published crime figure stays {{ m.raw }}.</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Markets — weekly close</h3>
  <span class="hint">Spot gold &amp; silver (USD/oz) from <a href="https://gold-api.com">gold-api.com</a>; Broad US Dollar Index from <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DTWEXBGS">FRED (DTWEXBGS)</a>.</span>
</div>
<div class="grid markets">
  {% for mk in markets %}
  <div class="tile">
    <div class="k">{{ mk.label }}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ mk.value|fmt(mk.unit) }}</div>
    {{ mk.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Week close</span>
      <span>
        {% if mk.delta is not none %}
          <span class="{{ 'delta-up' if mk.delta >= 0 else 'delta-down' }}">
            {{ "%+.2f"|format(mk.delta) }}% WoW
          </span>
        {% else %}
          —
        {% endif %}
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Short-term pulse</h3>
  <span class="hint">Faster-moving indicators outside the BugOut Index. Each tile shows the observation date and age. Source: <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org">FRED</a>.</span>
</div>
<div class="grid pulse">
  {% for p in pulse %}
  <div class="tile{% if p.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ p.label }}{% if p.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ p.value|fmt(p.unit) }}</div>
    {{ p.sparkline|safe }}
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/{{ p.source_id }}">{{ p.source_id }}</a></span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ p.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Labor utilization — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Prime-age (25–54) employment-population ratio and labor-force participation, monthly and seasonally adjusted, from BLS via FRED.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  These readings are companions only. They are not in the BugOut Index and they have no weight.
  Replacing headline unemployment still requires a backtest.
  {% if labor_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; values are carried forward from the {{ labor_reused_from }} publish. The dates below are the FRED observation dates.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid labor">
  {% for tile in labor_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 1) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">FRED {{ tile.source_id }}</a></span>
      <span>not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if labor_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ labor_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a FRED observation month, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title">
  <h3>Food prices — shadow series</h3>
  <span class="hint">Not in the BugOut Index. No weight. Food CPI, 12-month percent change, not seasonally adjusted, from BLS via FRED.</span>
</div>
<p class="rev-callout">
  This reading is a companion only. It is not in the BugOut Index and it has no weight.
  The figure is the public 12-month change in food prices
  (<a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/CPIUFDNS">FRED CPIUFDNS</a>,
  BLS <a href="https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CUUR0000SAF1?output_view=pct_12mths">CUUR0000SAF1</a>),
  rounded to one decimal the way BLS prints that table. It is not a score.
  {% if food_reused_from %}
  This week’s fetch failed; the value is carried forward from the {{ food_reused_from }} publish. The date below is the FRED observation date.
  {% endif %}
</p>
<div class="grid food">
  {% for tile in food_tiles %}
  <div class="tile{% if tile.stale %} stale{% endif %}">
    <div class="k">{{ tile.label }}{% if tile.stale %} <span class="badge-stale">Stale</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="v">{{ tile.value|fmt(tile.unit, 1) }}</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><a href="{{ tile.source_url }}">FRED {{ tile.source_id }}</a></span>
      <span>not in the BugOut Index</span>
    </div>
    <div class="age">{{ tile.age_text }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% if food_chart %}
<div class="chart-card">{{ food_chart|safe }}</div>
<p class="chart-caption">Each point is a FRED observation month, not a BugOut Index publication week. Not in the BugOut Index.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="section-title"><h3>About this index</h3></div>
<p style="max-width:70ch;color:var(--muted);">
  The BugOut Index is a directional stress and stability reading
  (methodology v{{ snapshot.methodology_version }}). Six published statistics sit between
  fixed endpoints and combine into one 0–100 score. Higher means those conditions are
  less stressed. The number shows how hard the published inputs are pressing. It is not
  a forecast, and it is not an instruction to bug out.
  Markets, the short-term pulse, labor utilization, and food prices on this page are companions.
  They are not in the score. Several inputs update monthly, quarterly, or once a year,
  so many weeks the number does not move.
  See <a href="./methodology.html">methodology</a> for the calculation, weights, and limits.
  The committed weekly files are the record of a past score. Rerunning the publisher
  fetches current observations and does not rebuild that week.
</p>
<p style="max-width:70ch;color:var(--muted);">
  For the long-horizon structural picture — whether the country is currently set up to
  produce broadly-shared prosperity and mobility over years and decades — see the
  <a href="https://adammontville.github.io/american-dream-reality-index/">American Dream Reality Index (ADRI)</a>.
  ADRI updates annually and weights toward education, health, real income, employment,
  inequality, and civic and safety fundamentals. The two indexes answer different
  questions. The BugOut Index is a weekly reading of pressure in a few published
  series. ADRI moves on slow structural conditions. Each can move for reasons the
  other does not catch.
</p>

{% endblock %}
